-- Fixes pokedex_moves.level_learned for moves that were spuriously pinned to level 1 by the
-- 2026-08-05 PokeAPI import (20260726150000_pokedex_learnset_moves.sql), found while investigating
-- Tropius's Leaf Storm (originally level_learned=1, a 5d12/1-per-day move -- much too strong for a
-- level-1 pick). Per the user's own two criteria, re-derived from live PokeAPI data
-- (pokeapi.co/api/v2/pokemon/{species}), not guessed:
--
-- [confirmed] rows: the SAME move shows a level > 1 in one game version and level 1 in another, for
-- the SAME species (e.g. Leaf Storm is level 61-71 in most Diamond-Pearl-through-Sword-Shield-era
-- games, but Scarlet-Violet's data shows an extra, spurious level-1 entry -- likely a move-reminder
-- eligibility artifact PokeAPI records alongside the real value in some games). Corrected to the
-- minimum level > 1 seen across that species' own version-group data. High confidence -- this is the
-- species' own real data, not an estimate.
--
-- [estimate] rows: no internal contradiction for this species (flat at level 1 in every game PokeAPI
-- has for it), but the SAME move is typically learned well past level 10 by every OTHER species that
-- knows it, AND this species is not an evolved form (an evolved form can legitimately carry a
-- pre-evolution move over at "level 1" the moment it evolves -- e.g. Basculegion inheriting a
-- Basculin-line move -- which isn't a bug, per the user's own refinement; excluded via
-- evolution_triggers.to_pokedex_id). Corrected to the lowest level any other species is recorded
-- learning that same move at, since no per-species ground truth exists for these -- an estimate, not
-- confirmed data, but preferred over leaving an outlier level-1 pick in place with no better answer.
--
-- Deliberately NOT touched: species/move pairs where every level-up appearance in every game is
-- level 1 (or level 0, meaning "learned automatically on evolution" per the import's own documented
-- convention) with no cross-version contradiction and no cross-species evidence the level is
-- unusual -- these have no evidence of being wrong. Also not touched: 13 rows for "Smoke screen"
-- (PokeAPI's actual slug is "smokescreen", one word, so the lookup silently missed it) -- a separate,
-- smaller gap left for its own pass.
